# NativeOrchestrator demo requests. Start SQL Server (docker compose up -d) and the app (dotnet run), then send
# each request with VS Code's REST Client or Visual Studio. Every start returns a statusUrl: poll it until the saga's
# status is Completed, Compensated or Failed. ApiManagementService (simulated in memory) holds the trigger values.
#
# The client saga also starts by itself every 5 minutes (schedule "client-every-5-minutes"), and only one runs at a
# time: if a scheduled run is active, the starts below answer 409, and if one of these is active, the occurrence is
# skipped. Each simulated operation takes a random 0-20 s.

@host = http://localhost:5080

### Client run: provisions, then synchronizes (Completed)
# @name run
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "correlationId": "client-manual-1",
  "data": { "runName": "client-manual-1" }
}

### Status
GET {{host}}{{run.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### History
GET {{host}}{{run.response.body.$.statusUrl}}/history

### Another run while the first is active: 409, outcome AlreadyRunning, with the running saga's ID
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "runName": "client-manual-2" } }

### Same correlation ID again: returns the existing saga ("created": false)
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "correlationId": "client-manual-1",
  "data": { "runName": "client-manual-1" }
}

### Provisioning fails: nothing succeeded, so nothing is compensated (Compensated, StepFailed)
# @name failProvision
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "runName": "FAIL-PROVISION manual" } }

###
GET {{host}}{{failProvision.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Synchronization fails: provisioning is reverted (Compensated, StepFailed)
# @name failSync
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "runName": "FAIL-SYNC manual" } }

###
GET {{host}}{{failSync.response.body.$.statusUrl}}

### Cancel a run while it waits (Compensated, Cancelled)
# @name cancelled
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "runName": "client-cancelled" } }

###
POST {{host}}{{cancelled.response.body.$.statusUrl}}/cancel

### Invalid data: 400
POST {{host}}/sagas/client
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "runName": "" } }

### Unknown saga type: 404
POST {{host}}/sagas/unknown
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": {} }

### Health (checks the saga database)
GET {{host}}/health
